          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "When navigating child custody disputes and parenting arrangements in Brisbane’s northern corridor, you will generally need a firm that can either **represent you** through negotiations and court, or act as an **independent, registered Family Dispute Resolution Practitioner (FDRP)** qualified to issue a Section 60I Certificate under the *Family Law Act 1975*.\n\nThe following family law practices in and around **Chermside** and **North Lakes** are well regarded for parenting disputes and dispute resolution:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Top Practices in Chermside**\n\n* **Barton Family Lawyers (Chermside)**\n  * **Location:** Directly opposite Westfield Chermside (Gympie Road).\n  * **Mediation & FDR Capability:** Practice Director **Courtney Barton** is both an experienced family lawyer and a **Nationally Accredited Mediator and Registered FDRP**.\n  * **Focus:** They handle parenting disputes, parenting plans, and high-conflict custody matters (such as cases involving parental alienation, domestic abuse, or coercive control). They offer fixed-fee mediation services.\n\n* **LGM Family Law (Chermside)**\n  * **Location:** Chermside (Gympie Road).\n  * **Focus:** LGM focuses heavily on parenting arrangements, child custody negotiations, and drafting legally binding Consent Orders. They frequently prepare clients for mediation and represent parents if disputes escalate toward the Federal Circuit and Family Court.\n\n* **Cudmore Legal (Aspley / Chermside Border)**\n  * **Location:** Aspley Hypermarket (just minutes north of Chermside).\n  * **Focus:** A dedicated family law firm handling parenting disputes, living arrangements, and interstate relocation disputes. They represent clients at mediations and provide strong advocacy if out-of-court options break down.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Top Practices in North Lakes**\n\n* **Best Wilson Buckley (BWB) Family Law (North Lakes)**\n  * **Location:** 1642 Anzac Avenue, North Lakes.\n  * **Mediation & FDR Capability:** Highly regarded specialist family law firm with **in-house accredited mediators and FDRPs**.\n  * **Focus:** They specialize exclusively in family law with an emphasis on child-focused dispute resolution, structured shuttle mediation, and long-term workable parenting arrangements. \n\n* **North Brisbane Law (North Lakes)**\n  * **Location:** Endeavour Boulevard, North Lakes.\n  * **Mediation & FDR Capability:** Principal **Tracey Mackenzie-Ross** is a long-standing family lawyer and a **Nationally Accredited Mediator**.\n  * **Focus:** They handle child custody, parenting plan drafting, grandparents’ rights, and dispute negotiations, aiming to keep families out of court whenever possible.\n\n* **ABA Lawyers (North Lakes)**\n  * **Location:** North Lakes.\n  * **Focus:** Known for alternative dispute resolution and complex parenting arrangements. They provide negotiation-first representation to formalize arrangements via parenting plans or consent orders.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Specialized Regional Mediators (Chermside/North Lakes Corridor)**\n\nIf you need a strictly neutral third party to conduct formal mediation:\n* **Future Family Dispute Resolution / Future Family Law (Aspley):** Led by **Selena James**, an accredited FDRP who facilitates parenting conferences and issues Section 60I certificates if discussions cannot reach agreement.\n\n---\n\n### **Important Consideration: Representation vs. Mediation**\n\nUnder Australian family law, **an accredited FDRP must remain impartial**. \n* If you hire a lawyer at one of these firms to **represent or advise you**, they **cannot** also act as the neutral mediator for your matter.\n* If you and the other parent jointly engage an accredited FDRP from a firm (such as Courtney Barton or BWB’s mediation panel), they are acting as the **neutral mediator** to guide agreement or issue a Section 60I certificate, and neither of you can use them as your personal legal counsel.",
